IMPORT prelude

-- Organised Crime Act 2015 (Singapore) -- what counts as an organised criminal group (s 2(1)), the membership and recruiting
-- offences (ss 5, 6), the enhanced punishments for instructing an offence and for committing one for a group (ss 7(4), (5), 13),
-- the limits on organised crime prevention orders and financial reporting orders (ss 17, 22, 26, 27), director disqualification
-- (s 39), tipping-off (s 44), the duty to give information (s 74) and composition (s 79).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/OCA2015.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 21 of 2025 (in force 30 December 2025, adding the scam-group offences) and, in the Schedule, S 560/2026 (in force
-- 17 August 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the Part 2 offences an ordinary person
-- could commit or be charged with, the sentence arithmetic, and the hard limits on the orders a court may make. Not encoded: the
-- grounds for making an OCPO or FRO (ss 15, 16, 21) beyond their duration, monitoring, variation, appeals, investigation powers
-- (Part 7), informer protection (ss 42, 43), confiscation of benefits (Part 9), examination orders (s 73), the list of serious
-- offences in Part 1 of the Schedule (taken as a given fact), ss 8 to 12 beyond their shared penalty, and s 76 (officers' liability).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Organised Crime Act 2015 -- offences and orders`

§§ `2(1) -- groups`

-- "group" means "a group of 3 or more individuals (whether or not ordinarily resident in Singapore), however organised".
-- "organised criminal group": a group that has as its only purpose, or one of its purposes, the obtaining of a financial or other
-- material benefit from the commission or facilitation by any person of (a) any serious offence; or (b) "any act outside Singapore
-- that, if the act occurred in Singapore, would constitute a serious offence".
-- "locally-linked organised criminal group": the same, but only limb (a) -- "any serious offence". AS DEPOSITED the definition has no
-- other local element: no requirement that a member, or the offence, be in Singapore.
-- The scam-group definitions (Act 21 of 2025) are the same with "serious scam offence" (Part 2 of the Schedule: Penal Code s 420(2)).
-- "serious offence" means any offence in Part 1 of the Schedule; that list is not encoded -- whether a purpose concerns a serious
-- offence is a given fact here.
DECLARE Group HAS
    `number of individuals` IS A NUMBER
    `seeks benefit from a serious offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `seeks benefit from a foreign act that would be a serious offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `seeks benefit from a serious scam offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `seeks benefit from a foreign act that would be a serious scam offence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a group` IF
    `the group`'s `number of individuals` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an organised criminal group` IF
    `it is a group` `the group`
    AND (    `the group`'s `seeks benefit from a serious offence`
         OR  `the group`'s `seeks benefit from a foreign act that would be a serious offence`)

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a locally-linked organised criminal group` IF
    `it is a group` `the group` AND `the group`'s `seeks benefit from a serious offence`

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an organised criminal scam group` IF
    `it is a group` `the group`
    AND (    `the group`'s `seeks benefit from a serious scam offence`
         OR  `the group`'s `seeks benefit from a foreign act that would be a serious scam offence`)

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a locally-linked organised criminal scam group` IF
    `it is a group` `the group` AND `the group`'s `seeks benefit from a serious scam offence`

-- The accused's state of mind about what the group is. Most Part 2 offences need "knowing or having reasonable grounds to
-- believe"; the scam limbs added by Act 21 of 2025 need "knowing" only.
DECLARE Accused HAS
    `is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows what the group is` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has reasonable grounds to believe what the group is` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the accused` IS AN Accused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `knows or has reasonable grounds` IF
    `the accused`'s `knows what the group is` OR `the accused`'s `has reasonable grounds to believe what the group is`

§§ `5 -- membership`

-- s 5(1): "Any person who is or acts as a member of a group, knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe that the group is a
-- locally-linked organised criminal group" -- fine up to $100,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 5(1A): the same for a locally-linked organised criminal scam group, but "knowing" only, and "shall also be punished with caning
-- with not less than 6 strokes".
-- s 5(2): factors a court may consider (meetings, dress, hand signs, tattoos, recruiting, initiation ceremony, ...) -- not encoded.
-- Membership is an offence only for a LOCALLY-LINKED group; there is no membership offence for an organised criminal group that is
-- only one under limb (b) (benefit from acts abroad).
GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the accused` IS AN Accused, `is or acts as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `membership is an offence under s 5(1)` IF
    `is or acts as a member` AND `it is a locally-linked organised criminal group` `the group` AND `knows or has reasonable grounds` `the accused`

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the accused` IS AN Accused, `is or acts as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `membership is an offence under s 5(1A)` IF
    `is or acts as a member` AND `it is a locally-linked organised criminal scam group` `the group` AND `the accused`'s `knows what the group is`

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the accused` IS AN Accused, `is or acts as a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minimum strokes of caning for membership` MEANS
    IF `membership is an offence under s 5(1A)` `the group` `the accused` `is or acts as a member` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `6 -- recruiting`

-- s 6(1): a person IN Singapore who incites, induces or invites another (or uses violence, threat or intimidation to do so) to become
-- a member of, or assist in managing, a group, knowing or having reasonable grounds to believe it is an ORGANISED criminal group.
-- s 6(2): a person OUTSIDE Singapore -- the same, but only for a LOCALLY-LINKED organised criminal group.
-- s 6(5), (6): the scam equivalents (Act 21 of 2025), "knowing" only.
GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the accused` IS AN Accused, `recruited someone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recruiting is an offence under the general limbs` IF
    `recruited someone` AND `knows or has reasonable grounds` `the accused`
    AND (    (`the accused`'s `is in Singapore` AND `it is an organised criminal group` `the group`)
         OR  ((NOT `the accused`'s `is in Singapore`) AND `it is a locally-linked organised criminal group` `the group`))

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the accused` IS AN Accused, `recruited someone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recruiting is an offence under the scam limbs` IF
    `recruited someone` AND `the accused`'s `knows what the group is`
    AND (    (`the accused`'s `is in Singapore` AND `it is an organised criminal scam group` `the group`)
         OR  ((NOT `the accused`'s `is in Singapore`) AND `it is a locally-linked organised criminal scam group` `the group`))

GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the accused` IS AN Accused, `recruited someone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recruiting is an offence` IF
       `recruiting is an offence under the general limbs` `the group` `the accused` `recruited someone`
    OR `recruiting is an offence under the scam limbs` `the group` `the accused` `recruited someone`

-- s 6(4), (8): higher maxima where A knows or has reasonable grounds to believe the recruit was "a vulnerable person or below 21 years
-- of age". s 6(9): if that is proved, A "is presumed, unless otherwise proven", to have known. So the aggravation falls away only if A
-- disproves knowledge.
GIVEN `recruit's age` IS A NUMBER, `recruit is a vulnerable person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused disproves knowing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recruiting is aggravated` IF
    (`recruit's age` LESS THAN 21 OR `recruit is a vulnerable person`) AND (NOT `the accused disproves knowing`)

-- s 6(3), (7): individual -- $250,000 or 5 years or both; any other case -- $500,000.
-- s 6(4), (8): individual -- $350,000 or 7 years or both; any other case -- $700,000.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `aggravated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum fine for recruiting` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `aggravated` THEN 350000 ELSE 250000
    ELSE IF `aggravated` THEN 700000 ELSE 500000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `aggravated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum years of imprisonment for recruiting` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `aggravated` THEN 7 ELSE 5
    ELSE 0

-- s 6(7)(a), (8)(a): an individual under the scam limbs "shall also be punished with caning with not less than 6 strokes". The
-- non-individual case carries a fine only. (INFERENCE: where conduct falls under both a general and a scam limb, this encoding takes
-- the scam limb's caning as applying; the text does not say which charge is brought.)
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `under the scam limbs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minimum strokes of caning for recruiting` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` AND `under the scam limbs` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `8 to 12 -- the shared penalty`

-- ss 8, 9, 10, 11: individual -- $250,000 or 5 years or both; any other case -- $500,000.
-- s 12 (facilitation): individual -- $100,000 or 5 years or both; any other case -- $200,000.
DECLARE SupportOffence IS ONE OF
    `procuring property for the group (s 8)`
    `applying property for the group (s 9)`
    `letting the group use premises (s 10)`
    `dealing in the group's property (s 11)`
    `facilitating the group's offence (s 12)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A SupportOffence, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum fine for supporting a group` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `facilitating the group's offence (s 12)` THEN IF `is an individual` THEN 100000 ELSE 200000
    OTHERWISE IF `is an individual` THEN 250000 ELSE 500000

§§ `13 -- committing an offence for a group`

-- s 13(1): a conviction in Singapore for an offence under any other written law (the predicate offence), proved to have been committed
-- at the direction of, or in furtherance of the illegal purpose of, a group the person knows or has reasonable grounds to believe is an
-- organised criminal group. s 13(2): committed outside Singapore -- a locally-linked organised criminal group.
GIVEN `the group` IS A Group, `the accused` IS AN Accused, `for the group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 13 enhancement applies` IF
    `for the group` AND `knows or has reasonable grounds` `the accused`
    AND (    (`the accused`'s `is in Singapore` AND `it is an organised criminal group` `the group`)
         OR  ((NOT `the accused`'s `is in Singapore`) AND `it is a locally-linked organised criminal group` `the group`))

-- s 13(3)(a): maximum fine is "twice the maximum amount of fine prescribed for the predicate offence".
-- (b): imprisonment of less than 4 years -- the maximum plus 2 years; (c): 4 years or more "(other than life imprisonment)" -- plus 5
-- years. s 13(4): minimum sentences are unaffected.
GIVEN `predicate maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`enhanced maximum fine under s 13` MEANS `predicate maximum fine` TIMES 2

GIVEN `predicate maximum years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`enhanced maximum years under s 13` MEANS
    IF `predicate maximum years` LESS THAN 4 THEN `predicate maximum years` PLUS 2 ELSE `predicate maximum years` PLUS 5

§§ `7(3) to (5) -- instructing an offence`

-- s 7(1), (2): instructing another to commit a Part 2 offence, or an offence the instructor knows is for an organised (or
-- locally-linked) criminal group. Punishment is that of the offence instructed, modified:
-- s 7(4), offence NOT committed: (a) fine -- twice the maximum; (b) imprisonment (other than life) -- "half of the maximum"; (c) death
-- or life -- replaced by imprisonment "which must not exceed 10 years"; (d) death or life AND hurt caused -- not exceeding 20 years.
-- s 7(5), offence committed: (a) fine -- 4 times; (b) imprisonment under 4 years -- plus 4 years; (c) 4 years or more (other than
-- life) -- plus 10 years. s 7(5) says nothing of death or life imprisonment.
GIVEN `the instructed offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN, `predicate maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum fine for instructing` MEANS
    IF `the instructed offence was committed` THEN `predicate maximum fine` TIMES 4 ELSE `predicate maximum fine` TIMES 2

GIVEN `predicate maximum years` IS A NUMBER, `death or life` IS A BOOLEAN, `hurt was caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum years for an instruction not carried out` MEANS
    IF `death or life`
    THEN IF `hurt was caused` THEN 20 ELSE 10
    ELSE `predicate maximum years` DIVIDED BY 2

GIVEN `predicate maximum years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum years for an instruction carried out` MEANS
    IF `predicate maximum years` LESS THAN 4 THEN `predicate maximum years` PLUS 4 ELSE `predicate maximum years` PLUS 10

§§ `17, 22, 26, 27 -- limits on OCPOs and FROs`

-- s 17(2): an OCPO "is not to be in force for more than 5 years beginning with the coming into force of the OCPO".
-- s 22(2): an FRO made under s 21(1) (application, no conviction) -- not more than 5 years. s 22(3): made under s 21(2) (on conviction)
-- -- not more than "the sentence of imprisonment imposed by the court for the offence ... plus 5 years".
-- s 27: neither may be made against an individual "below 16 years of age" at the time it is made.
GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the OCPO duration is permitted` IF `years` AT MOST 5

GIVEN `made on conviction` IS A BOOLEAN, `years of imprisonment imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`longest FRO in years` MEANS
    IF `made on conviction` THEN `years of imprisonment imposed` PLUS 5 ELSE 5

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an OCPO or FRO may be made against the individual` IF `age` AT LEAST 16

-- s 26(1), (3): failing without reasonable excuse to comply -- individual $10,000 or 3 years or both; any other case $20,000.
-- s 26(2): not excused on the ground that information "might tend to incriminate the person".
GIVEN `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `ground is self-incrimination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to comply is an offence` IF
    `failed to comply` AND ((NOT `has a reasonable excuse`) OR `ground is self-incrimination`)

§§ `39 -- director disqualification`

-- s 39(3): if sentenced to imprisonment, the disqualification "takes effect upon conviction and continues for a period of 5 years after
-- the person's release from prison". s 39(4): if not, 5 years, "or for a shorter period that the court may specify".
-- Here: years from conviction to the end of the disqualification. A specified period of 0 means none was specified.
GIVEN `imprisoned` IS A BOOLEAN, `years until release` IS A NUMBER, `period the court specified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`years of disqualification from conviction` MEANS
    IF `imprisoned` THEN `years until release` PLUS 5
    ELSE IF `period the court specified` GREATER THAN 0 AND `period the court specified` LESS THAN 5
         THEN `period the court specified`
         ELSE 5

§§ `44 -- tipping-off`

-- s 44(1): a person who knows or has reasonable grounds to suspect that a law enforcement officer is acting or proposing to act in an
-- investigation under the Act, and discloses information likely to prejudice it -- $30,000 or 3 years or both.
-- (2), (3): lawyers and legal counsel advising a client or for legal proceedings are exempt; (6) not if the disclosure is "with a view
-- to furthering any illegal purpose". (7): a defence "to prove that the person did not know and had no reasonable ground to suspect"
-- that the disclosure was likely to prejudice. (8): enforcement of the Act or other penal legislation is exempt.
GIVEN `suspects an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN, `disclosed prejudicial information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lawyer advising or litigating` IS A BOOLEAN, `to further an illegal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves no reason to suspect prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting in enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `tipping-off is an offence` IF
    `suspects an investigation` AND `disclosed prejudicial information`
    AND (NOT (`lawyer advising or litigating` AND (NOT `to further an illegal purpose`)))
    AND (NOT `proves no reason to suspect prejudice`)
    AND (NOT `acting in enforcement`)

§§ `74 -- duty to give information`

-- s 74(1): every person aware of information about the commission of, an arrangement facilitating, or another's intention to commit,
-- an offence under the Act must "immediately" give it to a law enforcement officer, absent reasonable excuse ("the burden of proving
-- which lies upon the person so aware"). (3): having already given it under another written law is a reasonable excuse.
-- (2): natural person -- $5,000 or 12 months or both; any other case -- $10,000.
GIVEN `aware of information` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave it immediately` IS A BOOLEAN, `already gave it under other law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves another reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to give information is an offence` IF
    `aware of information` AND (NOT `gave it immediately`)
    AND (NOT `already gave it under other law`) AND (NOT `proves another reasonable excuse`)

§§ `79 -- composition`

-- s 79(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for a sum not exceeding "the lower of" (a) one half of
-- the maximum fine prescribed for the offence and (b) $5,000. Which offences are prescribed is left to regulations (not retrieved).
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`largest composition sum` MEANS `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
